Subject: [PATCH 60/65] Kannada liveness texts reviewed by a native speaker: 2
 corrections and 1 suggestion (task 27)

The Kannada review of 2026-10-28 (both batches). The liveness term is confirmed correct by the reviewer
(it comes from the word for "alive"), so no other text changes. Texts are taken from the reviewer's files,
not retyped.
- The 2 corrections (rows marked N): liveness_status_passed and liveness_tips_capture_area (everyday words
  instead of the formal or technical ones).
- One optional suggestion adopted, to match Hindi: liveness_feedback_action_detected.
- Not adopted: the improve_lighting alternative (longer; the hint line stays short), the "more formal"
  variant of model_installed, and the loanword for "model" (the reviewer asked for one consistent choice;
  the current word stays everywhere).
- The review notes of app_kn.arb record the review; Arabic is the only language still pending.

Tests: liveness_l10n_test and model_bundle_test expect the Kannada review note. flutter test test/liveness:
325 passing, 20 skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
